Suppose you run:

ping google.com

And you get:

Temporary failure in name resolution

=> What does this mean?

It means Ubuntu is not able to convert google.com into its IP address.

For example:

google.com  →  IP address

DNS does this conversion.

Important: This error does not always mean that the internet is completely down.

There could be different reasons:

DNS server is not reachable
DNS configuration is incorrect
Network connection is not working
DNS service has a problem

=> How to troubleshoot?

First, try pinging an IP address directly:

ping -c 3 8.8.8.8

Then try the domain name:

ping -c 3 google.com

=> Understand the result

If:

ping 8.8.8.8       → Works ✅
ping google.com    → Fails ❌

Then:

Internet/network may be working
        ↓
But DNS name resolution is failing
        ↓
Possible DNS problem
